@*
    DEAD MARKUP. NOT INCLUDED BY ANY PAGE. DO NOT BUILD ON THIS FILE.

    The narrative Impact Details feature was withdrawn -- see the banner
    on Api/Models/RiskImpactDetailModels.cs. risk-centre.cshtml no longer
    includes this partial or impact-detail-form.js, and the endpoints the
    script calls are gone. Delete both files together.

    THE Impact Details form -- add / edit one recorded consequence of a
    risk, against an obligation or against the risk as a whole.

    Driven by wwwroot/js/Shared/impact-detail-form.js. Include this
    partial once on a page, load that script, and any screen on that page
    can open the same dialog.

    WHY IT IS SHARED FROM THE START
    -------------------------------
    Migration 309 added Impact Details for FIVE pages: Risk Analysis,
    View Risk, Residual Analysis, Accept and Review. Two of them can
    ADD (Risk Analysis and Review), and the requirement is explicit that
    Review "use the same Impact Details fields, validation, popup/modal
    and API/database structure already used in Risk Analysis".

    So the form is a shared component before it has a second caller,
    rather than being copied into the second page later -- which is what
    _task-form-dialog.cshtml and _obligation-form-dialog.cshtml both had
    to be extracted to fix. See docs/risk-obligation-structure.md.

    THE FIELD SET
    -------------
    Impact area* - Description* - Severity - Affected party -
    Estimated value - Time horizon - Remarks.

    Only the first two are required, and Severity is deliberately
    optional: an impact worth recording before it has been sized is a real
    state, and demanding a level would invite a guessed one.

    Severity is the SAME risk_impact_master the inherent and residual
    scores use, so "impact" means one thing in this product. The host
    passes the options it has already loaded rather than this dialog
    fetching a second copy.

    NOT A <form>
    ------------
    A `<form method="dialog">` submits on Enter in any text input, which
    closes the dialog and throws the half-typed impact away. Every button
    is type="button" and the save is a fetch. Same reason the obligation
    form uses a div, and no backdrop dismissal for the same reason
    either: Cancel is the only way out.

    SELF-CONTAINED STYLES
    ---------------------
    Every class is `gid-` prefixed and defined below. The risk pages
    style their own panels through .risk-* and .ra-* rules scoped to
    those pages; a dialog that borrowed them would render differently
    depending on which of the five pages opened it.

    Included ONCE per page. The ids are global, which is what lets any
    screen on that page open the same dialog.
*@
<dialog class="gid" id="gidDialog" aria-labelledby="gidHeading">
  <div class="gid-form">
    <header class="gid-head">
        <div>
            <h2 id="gidHeading">Add impact detail</h2>
            @* Which obligation this is being recorded against, or the
               risk itself. Read-only: it is decided by the button that
               opened the dialog, not chosen here -- picking it twice is
               how an impact ends up filed under the wrong obligation. *@
            <p class="gid-note" id="gidContext"></p>
        </div>
        <button class="pm-modal-close" id="gidClose" type="button" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    </header>

    <div class="gid-msg" id="gidMsg"></div>

    <div class="gid-body">
        @* 0 adds; the row id edits. The server echoes back the id it
           wrote even on a failed save, so a retry edits that row instead
           of inserting a second one. *@
        <input type="hidden" id="gidId" value="0">

        <div class="gid-grid">
            <label class="gid-field">
                <span class="gid-label">Impact area<i class="gid-req">*</i></span>
                <select id="gidArea"><option value="">-- select --</option></select>
            </label>

            <label class="gid-field">
                <span class="gid-label">Severity</span>
                <select id="gidSeverity"><option value="">-- not sized yet --</option></select>
                <span class="gid-hint">The same scale as the risk score. Leave blank until it is known.</span>
            </label>

            <label class="gid-field gid-span2">
                <span class="gid-label">Description<i class="gid-req">*</i></span>
                <textarea id="gidDescription" rows="4" maxlength="4000"
                          placeholder="What actually happens, and to what."></textarea>
            </label>

            <label class="gid-field">
                <span class="gid-label">Affected party</span>
                <input type="text" id="gidAffected" maxlength="300"
                       placeholder="A customer segment, a regulator, a team" />
            </label>

            <label class="gid-field">
                <span class="gid-label">Estimated value</span>
                <input type="text" id="gidEstimated" maxlength="120"
                       placeholder="e.g. 2 days downtime, ~200 records" />
                @* Free text, not money: four of the nine impact areas
                   have no currency value at all. *@
                <span class="gid-hint">Free text -- not every impact is a number.</span>
            </label>

            <label class="gid-field">
                <span class="gid-label">Time horizon</span>
                <select id="gidHorizon">
                    <option value="">-- not set --</option>
                    <option value="Immediate">Immediate</option>
                    <option value="ShortTerm">Short term</option>
                    <option value="MediumTerm">Medium term</option>
                    <option value="LongTerm">Long term</option>
                </select>
            </label>

            <label class="gid-field gid-span2">
                <span class="gid-label">Remarks</span>
                <textarea id="gidRemarks" rows="2" maxlength="1000"></textarea>
            </label>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="gid-foot">
        <button class="pm-button primary" id="gidSave" type="button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> Save impact
        </button>
        <button class="pm-button" id="gidCancel" type="button">Cancel</button>
        <span class="gid-note" id="gidStage"></span>
    </footer>
  </div>
</dialog>

<style>
    /* Scoped to .gid so nothing here reaches another dialog, and so the
       dialog does not depend on which page included it. */
    .gid {
        width: min(760px, calc(100vw - 32px));
        max-height: calc(100vh - 64px);
        padding: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 10px;
        background: #fff; color: var(--grac-ink, #25345a);
        box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, .25);
    }
    .gid::backdrop { background: rgba(15, 23, 42, .45); }

    .gid-form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; max-height: calc(100vh - 64px); }

    .gid-head {
        display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px;
        padding: 12px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grac-line, #e2e7f0);
    }
    .gid-head > div { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
    .gid-head h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }

    /* The only part that scrolls, so Save stays reachable on a short
       viewport however long the description gets. */
    .gid-body { padding: 14px 16px; overflow-y: auto; }

    .gid-foot {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
        padding: 12px 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--grac-line, #e2e7f0);
        background: #f8fafc;
    }

    .gid-msg {
        display: none; margin: 10px 16px 0;
        padding: 7px 11px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 12px;
    }

    /* Two columns; the long-form fields take the whole row. */
    .gid-grid {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 10px 14px; align-items: start;
    }
    .gid-span2 { grid-column: span 2; }

    .gid-field { display: block; min-width: 0; }
    .gid-label {
        display: block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--grac-muted, #758095); margin-bottom: 3px;
    }
    .gid-req { color: #dc2626; font-style: normal; margin-left: 2px; }
    .gid-note { margin: 2px 0 0; font-size: 11px; color: var(--grac-muted, #758095); }
    .gid-hint { display: block; margin-top: 3px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--grac-muted, #758095); }

    .gid-field input[type="text"],
    .gid-field select,
    .gid-field textarea {
        width: 100%; padding: 6px 8px;
        border: 1px solid var(--grac-line, #cbd5e1); border-radius: 4px;
        font: inherit; font-size: 13px; color: var(--grac-ink, #0f172a);
        background: #fff;
    }
    .gid-field textarea { resize: vertical; }

    /* One column on a narrow window: below this the pairs stop helping
       and start cramping. */
    @@media (max-width: 640px) {
        .gid-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
        .gid-span2 { grid-column: span 1; }
    }
</style>
